  <para style="p"> <verse style="v" number="13" /><char style="w" strong="G1722">By</char> <char style="w" strong="G3588">-</char> <char style="w" strong="G3004">speaking of</char> <char style="w" strong="G2537">a new [covenant]</char>,<note style="f" caller="+"><char style="fr">8:13 </char><char style="ft">Literally </char><char style="fqa">In saying new</char><char style="ft">; here and in <ref loc="HEB 9:1">Hebrews 9:1</ref> and 18, </char><char style="fqa">covenant </char><char style="ft">is included for clarity but is not contained in the Greek. A broader interpretation could also include </char><char style="fqa">priesthood </char><char style="ft">or </char><char style="fqa">tabernacle</char><char style="ft">.</char></note> <char style="w" strong="G3822">He has made</char> <char style="w" strong="G3588">the</char> <char style="w" strong="G4413">first one {obsolete}</char>; <char style="w" strong="G1161">and</char> <char style="w" strong="G3588">what</char> <char style="w" strong="G3822">is obsolete</char> <char style="w" strong="G2532">and</char> <char style="w" strong="G1095">aging</char> <char style="w" strong="G1451">will soon</char> <char style="w" strong="G854">disappear</char>.</para>
